record legeos.work.alt-tab-and-task-rail-icons-20261004/1 : work {
    title "Alt+Tab lists every open window and commits on release; the task island and Apps rail wear application icons instead of letters"
    state active
    scope [
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/chrome/**",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/input.rs",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/keybindings.rs",
        path "crates/templar-window/src/service.rs",
        path "crates/templar-window/src/switch.rs",
        path "crates/templar-window/src/task.rs",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/icons.rs",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/surface/app.rs",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/surface/bar_screen.rs",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/surface/offscreen.rs",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/taskbar.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        User request (2026-10-04, from Lubuntu, so nothing could be run in the live session): improve the window manager's bottom-gesture task viewer, especially icons instead of text labels, and make Alt+Tab properly reflect the open windows. Alt+Tab: WindowService::recent() and task::RECENT_MAX=7 are gone; WindowService::alt_tab_order() lists every mapped Application window, parked included, by last_activated. The walk is frozen at the first press; Tab/Shift+Tab only move the HUD selection; releasing Alt (or Super) activates it via commit_switch_walk (unparking a parked one); Escape (swallowed), a pointer press, another chord, Taskfield or Home reveal cancel via cancel_switch_walk; destroy/unmap prune the window from the ring (SwitchRing::remove); the pressure-overlay path now tracks chord_held. HUD rows (chrome::SwitcherEntry) show title -> application short name -> '(untitled)', parked rows in muted ink, and a scrolled window of rows (layout::switcher_visible_rows) when they do not fit. Alt+` (task::within_unit) now includes parked members. Icons: icons::load_app_icon_hinted tries every name from app_icon_names (Icon=, then the desktop file's own stem in its case and lower-cased) and the first that resolves and decodes wins; ensure_icon remembers lookups made before the application catalogue arrived (icon_hintless) and repeats them with the manifest's hints when DataUpdate::Apps lands; a group chip wears its most recently activated member's icon and each fan card its own window's (EntryWindow::app_id); the chip icon is centred in its 48-px cell; --render-bar/--render-rails load real icons from the machine's themes.
        """
    note """
        Uncommitted on developer-edition-0-1 over 2bc8f74, alongside the user's own WIP. Remaining checks are manual and need the installed TemplarOS session (deploy is the user's). Deviations from the brief: a key the pressure overlay takes cancels a walk rather than committing; modifier presses (Shift) no longer cancel a walk; the compositor HUD still draws no icons (the compositor loads none — a shell-drawn switcher over Layer::Presentation, as Taskfield's labels are, would be the route). The all-initials bar's cause in the installed session is still unconfirmed: the shell logs icon misses only at debug level and its ANSI output is stored as byte arrays in the journal.
        """
    acceptance {
        check headless-rail-icons {
            statement """
                templar-shell --render-rails against the TemplarOS root's data dirs draws the installed applications' chips as their icons, centred, with a letter only for an application that has no icon.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.task-rail-icons-headless-render-20261004 ]
        }
        check session-alt-tab-commits-on-release {
            statement """
                In the installed session: a quick Alt+Tab switches to the previous window; walking past three windows raises none of them until Alt is released, then only the selected one is activated (a parked one comes back); Alt+Shift+Tab walks backwards with Shift pressed mid-walk; Escape while Alt is held closes the HUD and changes nothing and the focused client receives no Escape; a click mid-walk closes the HUD without switching.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check session-alt-tab-lists-every-window {
            statement """
                In the installed session with nine or more application windows open, two of them parked: holding Alt and tapping Tab shows every one of them in the compositor HUD, newest first, the parked ones dimmed, and the list scrolls to keep the selection visible; no blank rows.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check session-alt-tab-window-closes-mid-walk {
            statement """
                In the installed session: closing a window (e.g. a terminal exiting on a timer) while Alt is held removes its HUD row, and releasing activates a live window; the HUD never stays on screen after Alt is up, including after the pressure overlay appeared mid-walk.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check session-rail-and-island-wear-icons {
            statement """
                In the installed session, after login and again after a shell restart (it restarts on its own), the Apps rail opened by the bottom-centre gesture and the island show each running application's icon (kitty, Firefox, Files, Settings, mpv), a window group shows its most recent member's icon, and the fan cards fall back to each window's own icon; any application still drawn as a letter is recorded with its canonical app id and the debug 'no icon resolved' line (RUST_LOG=templar_shell=debug).
                """
            method manual
        }
        check unit-tests {
            statement """
                The window model, compositor, shell and types test suites pass, covering alt_tab_order with more than seven and parked windows, ring pruning, step/commit/cancel on a check-backend state, HUD row windowing, icon-name fallbacks and group/fan-card icon keys.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -q -p templar-window -p templar-comp -p templar-shell -p templar-types"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.alt-tab-task-rail-icons-tests-20261004 ]
        }
    }
    implements [ @legeos.decision.task-system-four-scales-one-model ]
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.developer-edition-0-1 ]
    verified_by [
        @legeos.evidence.alt-tab-task-rail-icons-clippy-20261004,
        @legeos.evidence.alt-tab-task-rail-icons-tests-20261004,
        @legeos.evidence.task-rail-icons-headless-render-20261004
    ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.application-integration-interim/1 : work {
    title "Interim application integration — the Terminal role and the Super+grave drop-down terminal, the Files context menu, the search panel with FSearch as the FileSearch provider, Kitty defaults"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "apps/lege-files/**",
        path "compositor/lege-comp/src/keybindings.rs",
        path "crates/lege-appd/**",
        path "crates/lege-session-core/**",
        path "crates/lege-types/src/action.rs",
        path "crates/lege-types/src/provider.rs",
        path "debian/**",
        path "distro/**",
        path "services/lege-sessiond/**",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Integration choices the user made on 2026-09-03, revised the same day. (a) Terminal: ProviderRole::Terminal, exclusive, candidates from TerminalEmulator desktop entries, default kitty; the shell relays the selection with lege_shell_manager_v1.set_terminal and answers terminal_requested by launching the provider through the launch chain; Super+grave (compositor chord; a bare ~ or ` is a typed character and cannot be a global chord) toggles the terminal: launch when none, unshelve/activate when shelved or unfocused, shelve and refocus the previous window when focused, never close. No Ctrl+Alt+T. 'Open terminal here' in the Files context menu launches it with --directory. /etc/xdg/kitty/kitty.conf shipped by legeos-shell with the LegeOS palette, background_opacity 0.85, remember_window_size no, wayland_titlebar_color system, overridable by ~/.config/kitty. (b) Files object: secondary-click menu on rows and empty space reusing surface/context_menu.rs and the declared files.* verbs (Open, Open with…, Open terminal here, Copy path, Rename, Move to trash, Properties; New folder, Paste, Select all, Sort by…, Show hidden), then multi-select, keyboard verbs, drag-and-drop and properties-as-pane. (c) Search: the top field on Home stays the application launcher only (COSMIC's launcher shape); real search is the Files object's search field expanded into a partial-screen panel (about two thirds of the field, centred, hairline edge) over lege-filed's scoped index with path, size and modified time per row and keyboard navigation, whose last row is 'Search everywhere with FSearch'; ProviderRole::FileSearch, exclusive, default FSearch, launched with --search <query>; 'Search here…' in the context menu; lege-filed keeps its index; later sessiond feeds fsearch's include list from Files.Search1.Roots.
        """
    note """
        Plan text: docs/planning/window-groups-and-application-integration.md §4.2–4.6 (ea9810e). Implementation started 2026-09-03 in one lane: Terminal role → set_terminal/terminal_requested relay → Files context menu → search panel + FileSearch role → kitty.conf → multi-select if time. Terminal=true desktop-entry wrapping and Super+F are deferred. Not planned: reading fsearch's database or replacing Files.Search1.
        """
    depends_on [ @legeos.work.wayland-clipboard-and-dnd-transport ]
    implements [ @legeos.decision.the-home-field-is-a-launcher-not-a-search ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-surface-usability-next ]
}

record legeos.work.application-integration-interim/2 : work {
    title "Interim application integration — the Terminal role and the Super+grave drop-down terminal, the Files context menu, the search panel with FSearch as the FileSearch provider, Kitty defaults"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "apps/lege-files/**",
        path "compositor/lege-comp/src/keybindings.rs",
        path "crates/lege-appd/**",
        path "crates/lege-session-core/**",
        path "crates/lege-types/src/action.rs",
        path "crates/lege-types/src/provider.rs",
        path "debian/**",
        path "distro/**",
        path "services/lege-sessiond/**",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Integration choices the user made on 2026-09-03, revised later the same day. (a) Terminal: ProviderRole::Terminal, exclusive, candidates from TerminalEmulator desktop entries, default kitty; the shell relays the selection with lege_shell_manager_v1.set_terminal and answers terminal_requested by launching the provider through the launch chain; Super+grave (compositor chord; a bare ~ or ` is a typed character and cannot be a global chord) toggles the terminal: launch when none, unshelve/activate when shelved or unfocused, shelve and refocus the previous window when focused, never close. No Ctrl+Alt+T. 'Open terminal here' in the Files context menu launches it with --directory. /etc/xdg/kitty/kitty.conf shipped by legeos-shell with the LegeOS palette, background_opacity 0.85, remember_window_size no, wayland_titlebar_color system, overridable by ~/.config/kitty. (b) Files object: secondary-click menu on rows and empty space reusing surface/context_menu.rs and the declared files.* verbs (Open, Open with…, Open terminal here, Copy path, Rename, Move to trash, Properties; New folder, Paste, Select all, Sort by…, Show hidden), then multi-select, keyboard verbs, drag-and-drop and properties-as-pane. (c) Search: the top field on Home stays the application launcher only (COSMIC's launcher shape); real search is the Files object's search field expanded into a partial-screen panel (about two thirds of the field, centred, hairline edge) over lege-filed's scoped index with path, size and modified time per row and keyboard navigation, whose last row is 'Search everywhere with FSearch'; ProviderRole::FileSearch, exclusive, launched with --search <query>; 'Search here…' in the context menu. The later indexing direction replaces the interim two-database arrangement: lege-filed owns one persistent, incrementally maintained derived file index used by integrated Files search, a remote-index FSearch fork, Silvaview-rs, the CLI and future clients.
        """
    note """
        The application-integration plan remains docs/planning/window-groups-and-application-integration.md for terminal, Files UI and provider work. Its section 4.2 statements that fsearch keeps a second database and Files.Search1 is not replaced are superseded by the user's later 2026-09-03 direction and docs/planning/shared-incremental-file-index.md. The detailed implementation is tracked by @legeos.work.shared-incremental-file-index.
        """
    depends_on [ @legeos.work.wayland-clipboard-and-dnd-transport ]
    implements [ @legeos.decision.the-home-field-is-a-launcher-not-a-search ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-surface-usability-next ]
    supersedes [ @legeos.work.application-integration-interim/1 ]
}

