record legeos.work.compositor-knows-home-cards-park-motion-20261004/1 : work {
    title "The compositor learns where each window's Home card is (set_minimize_target, protocol v12) and shrinks a parked window into it, growing it back out on restore"
    state active
    scope [
        path "compositor/COMPOSITOR.md",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/motion.rs",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/protocols_shell.rs",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/scene.rs",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/space_sync.rs",
        path "interfaces/wayland/README.md",
        path "interfaces/wayland/templar-shell-v1.xml",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/surface/app.rs",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/surface/field_screen.rs",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/wayland_bridge.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        User request (2026-10-04): 'Why doesnt the compositor know where the cards are? That should be improved.' The Home work cards were shell pixels only, so parking was an instant cut. Protocol: templar_shell_manager_v1, the toplevel list and templar_shell_toplevel_v1 all move to v12 (toplevels are created at the manager's version, so only a manager-version gate can tell the shell the request exists); new templar_shell_toplevel_v1.set_minimize_target(surface, x, y, w, h), surface-local logical px on the shell's own Home surface, null or empty clears, a hint only. Shell: FieldScreen::work_targets (card rect per window, overflow windows -> the overflow card), app.rs sends only changes after each Home frame (Home is redrawn on every toplevel change, revealed or not), stops for a pre-v12 compositor. Compositor: protocols_shell stores per window (Home surface WindowId, local rect), refusing foreign or popup surfaces; motion.rs (200 ms ease-out, Park fades 1.0->0.3, Unpark the reverse, content centred in the card); space_sync::sync_after_change, the resync every park/restore route ends in, compares parked/visible state and starts motions; scene draws the moving window's surface tree without chrome at its stacking position; no new timers, finished motions pruned per frame. No card, lock, Taskfield, or Home not on screen means no motion, exactly as before.
        """
    note """
        Uncommitted on developer-edition-0-1 over 2bc8f74 with the user's WIP (which had already taken the manager to v11). Seen once in a nested winit session on the Lubuntu X11 host: a parked GTK probe drew faded, chromeless and displaced toward its card mid-motion. The restore direction, the feel of 200 ms/0.3 alpha, the DRM backend's frame pacing during motion and a park from the Home card's Park chip were not observed.
        """
    acceptance {
        check automated {
            statement """
                Compositor, window-model and shell tests and clippy pass, covering the motion maths, the target store and its refusals, park/unpark motion starts and teardown, and the shell's target diffing.
                """
            method command
            command "CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/tmp/legeos-clippy-target cargo test -q -p templar-comp -p templar-window -p templar-shell"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.card-targets-park-motion-tests-20261004 ]
        }
        check nested-park-motion {
            statement """
                In a nested session a parked window is drawn shrinking and fading toward its Home card before it disappears, with no compositor or shell errors.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.card-targets-park-motion-nested-20261004 ]
        }
        check session-no-motion-cases {
            statement """
                In the installed session: with the session locked, inside the window overview, or with Home hidden behind a fullscreen window, parking and restoring are instant as before; restarting the shell (it restarts itself) re-sends the cards and motion resumes.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check session-park-into-card {
            statement """
                In the installed session (DRM backend): parking a window by its minimize tag, Ctrl+Alt+P, the bar, or an application's own minimize shrinks it smoothly into its Home card's position over about 200 ms with no stutter or cursor freeze; a window behind the overflow card shrinks into that card.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check session-restore-from-card {
            statement """
                In the installed session: revealing Home and clicking a parked window's card grows the window back out of the card to its old place; its title band appears when it lands; input goes to it normally afterwards.
                """
            method manual
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @legeos.work.home-work-centred-folder-clusters-20261004 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.developer-edition-0-1 ]
    verified_by [
        @legeos.evidence.card-targets-park-motion-nested-20261004,
        @legeos.evidence.card-targets-park-motion-tests-20261004
    ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.compositor-window-authority/1 : work {
    title "The compositor's window authority: typed layers, one scene, explicit minimisation, recovery without the shell"
    state superseded
    scope [ path "compositor/**", path "crates/lege-window/**", path "interfaces/wayland/**" ]
    intent """
        Make lege-window the thing that decides stacking and geometry rather than a set of helpers: typed overlay layers as a total order with rules about which client may claim which layer; the one-workspace invariant as a type-level property, with deterministic migration when an output is removed and validation of restored geometry against the current topology; explicit minimisation to a Window Shelf that is always restorable to a recoverable geometry; a compositor-owned recovery band, a show-all-windows scatter and an escape route out of fullscreen that all work when the shell is dead; drag anchors held in one global logical coordinate space across mixed-scale outputs; window commands gated on activation grants with recent-input evidence; and property tests over generated multi-output topologies. lege-comp-integration keeps the render thread off D-Bus, hardens the identity cache against PID reuse, and tells the governor which instance the user is looking at.
        """
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.m1-session-runtime ]
}

