    ]
    intent """
        Three defects in one loop. (1) services/lege-resourced/src/daemon.rs run_loop arms the PSI trigger on session.slice, but scan.rs governs app.slice, a sibling, so application pressure does not wake the loop: arm a trigger whose scope includes the managed app.slice (its own trigger, or the parent user@ service scope). (2) While Normal the loop always waits the 60 s IDLE_HEARTBEAT even when PressureWait has no usable trigger, and the fallback then sleeps the whole timeout: with no healthy trigger, keep the configured active interval. (3) psi.rs Trigger::wait maps POLLERR/HUP/NVAL and non-EINTR errors to Timeout and returns at once, so a persistently failed descriptor spins: on such a result disable the trigger and fall back to the clock. Tests: deterministic scheduling tests for healthy, fallback and failed-trigger states, and a hung-up descriptor test; the existing pipe MSG_OOB test does not exercise POLLPRI when send fails, so replace or supplement it.
        """
    note "Astra rank P1, implement first. Replay fixtures must be untouched by the wait change: the decision path is unchanged, only when the loop wakes.\nThe committed supported legacy scope migration changed this planning head after its older completion evidence. Historical observations remain intact; this head is active for fresh acceptance evidence, not because a new code regression was observed. Live authority relations follow current heads rather than retired revisions."
    acceptance {
        check trigger-scope {
            statement """
                A test asserts the armed memory.pressure path is an ancestor of, or equal to, the governed app.slice path.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-resourced daemon"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.effectiveness-1-scoped-tests-20260909/1 ]
        }
        check wait-scheduling {
            statement """
                Unit tests show: a healthy trigger waits the idle heartbeat while Normal; no trigger waits the active interval; a failed descriptor is disabled after its first error result and the loop falls back to the clock instead of returning immediately.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-resourced psi"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.effectiveness-1-scoped-tests-20260909/1 ]
        }
    }
    derived_from [
        @legeos.assessment.astra-memory-polling-indexing-review-20260909#governor-wake
    ]
    implements [ @legeos.decision.resourced-separate-process ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.memory-polling-indexing-effectiveness-20260909 ]
    supersedes [ @legeos.work.governor-wake-reliability-20260909/2 ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.hands-on-fixes-20261007/1 : work {
    title "Hands-on 2026-10-07: Alt+Tab shown while held, a bar row of separate cards with parked windows, larger chip icons, draggable Home cards, PCManFM-Qt icons and Terminal role"
    state active
    scope [
        path "cli/templar/**",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/**",
        path "crates/templar-session-core/**",
        path "crates/templar-window/**",
        path "debian/**",
        path "docs/architecture/**",
        path "services/templar-sessiond/**",
        path "shell/templar-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        User request 2026-10-07 from the installed TemplarOS session. (1) Alt+Tab appeared for one frame and could not be cycled: the shell's Layer::Presentation switcher surface was hidden by WindowService::is_visible outside Taskfield while the compositor's text HUD stood down for any mapped Presentation surface; the walk is now a WindowService state (set_switch_walk) that shows the surface, and the text HUD yields only to a visible one; every switcher row is titled. (2) The bottom bar's second row stacked windows over each other and kitty got no row: the overlapping fan becomes a row of separate titled cards, and a unit's parked windows (terminals put away by the drop-down chord) count toward the row, never toward the Taskfield handover. (3) Bar chip icons 30% larger (26 to 34 px; chips 40 px tall). (4) Homegarden work cards open on release and can be dragged to free cells, kept as an in-memory pin plus the persisted per-folder hint, never a field tile. (5) PCManFM-Qt showed no icons (FallbackIconThemeName=oxygen, not installed) and launched xterm (not installed): templar-terminal launches the Terminal role provider through sessiond in the folder, /etc/xdg default and a sessiond start-up repair rewrite only invalid Terminal/FallbackIconThemeName values. (6) Rebuild every package so the next login runs the new modules.
        """
    note """
        Code, tests, nested and headless proofs are on the uncommitted tree over 7c68786; all TemplarOS debs were rebuilt into target/debian for the owner's scripts/reinstall-templaros-desktop.sh --skip-build (sudo) and next login. The installed-session check stays open until then. The bar's overlapping fan is replaced by a row of separate cards at the owner's request.
        """
    acceptance {
        check alt-tab-walk-shown {
            statement """
                In a nested compositor+shell, holding Alt and pressing Tab keeps the shell's Presentation surface in Space for the whole walk, the selection moves with each Tab, and releasing commits and removes it.
                """
            method command
            command "scripts/nested-session.sh start --no-daemons; two kitty clients; scripts/nested-session.sh input key 56 down / key 15 down|up / snapshot"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-20261007-nested-alt-tab/1 ]
        }
        check bar-row-and-icons {
            statement """
                templar-window and templar-shell tests pass, including the row's non-overlap assertion, the parked-window row/restore test and chip_action's parked/handover rules; the headless open-row render shows separate titled cards.
                """
            method command
            command "scripts/cargo-native.sh test -p templar-window -p templar-shell"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-20261007-tests/1 ]
        }
        check home-card-drag {
            statement """
                templar-shell tests cover press-release opening, a drag past the lift threshold moving a card to free cells without opening it, the drop surviving window churn, and invalid drops or Escape snapping back.
                """
            method command
            command "scripts/cargo-native.sh test -p templar-shell work_layout field_screen"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-20261007-tests/1 ]
        }
        check installed-session {
            statement """
                After the owner reinstalls the rebuilt packages and logs in again: Alt+Tab shows the shell switcher while held and cycles; the bar row shows separate cards including parked kitty windows; chip icons are larger; Home cards drag; PCManFM-Qt draws folder icons and opens a kitty terminal in the folder.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check pcmanfm-terminal-and-icons {
            statement """
                templar-session-core pcmanfm repair tests pass; templar terminal launches the Terminal role provider in a given directory through Launcher1; the user's settings.conf names templar-terminal and an installed icon theme.
                """
            method command
            command "scripts/cargo-native.sh test -p templar-session-core pcmanfm && templar terminal --dry-run"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-20261007-pcmanfm-terminal/1 ]
        }
    }
    derived_from [
        @legeos.observation.shell-switcher-surface-hidden-outside-taskfield-20261007
    ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.desktop-polish-and-test-infrastructure-backlog-20261004 ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.hands-on-run-2-fixes/1 : work {
    title "Act on the second hands-on run: adjustable windows, visible tiling, body-drag tiles, concise labels, a route to drives, one Settings widget"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "apps/lege-files/**",
        path "apps/lege-settings/**",
        path "compositor/lege-comp/**",
        path "crates/lege-types/**",
        path "crates/lege-window/**",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Fix every deficiency in @legeos.observation.hands-on-run-20260831-findings. (1) Windows are adjustable: the compositor's recovery-band move and corner-grip resize actually start their grabs (they previously demanded an implicit grab that cannot exist yet at band-press time, so both affordances were dead on real hardware). (2) New windows are placed — centred in the usable area, cascaded, size-clamped — instead of honouring a meaningless (0,0) request flush into the corner. (3) Arranging from the Home menu ends the reveal so the result is visible, and arranging with no windows open says so on the field. (4) Object-like tiles (file, folder, pane, app) drag-move from anywhere in their body; instrument tiles keep the band. (5) Browse rows and grids drop the FOLDER/FILE caption noise: the name leads, '/' marks a folder, extensions name files once, folders read as the folder material. (6) The browse toolbar's path is a clickable breadcrumb and a Files button hands the folder to org.legeos.Files with its drives sidebar. (7) The battery/volume/brightness widgets consolidate into ONE Settings widget whose click opens the Settings app, per the user's direct instruction.
        """
    note """
        All seven items are implemented and merged at ad3460b (my commits d79602f..49d999f plus the agent's bf75959..c5a4a0b); every command check passes there and the live nested session confirmed centred placement and oversize clamping. The one open check is #hands-on-confirmation — the user's next login at a real seat: window opens centred, band-move and grip-resize work, tiling menu visibly arranges, tiles drag-move, the Settings widget opens Settings. The packages must be rebuilt and reinstalled first (scripts/reinstall-legeos-desktop.sh, interactive sudo).
        """
    acceptance {
        check body-drag {
            statement """
                Object-like tiles arm a drag from anywhere in their body while widget tiles only grab by their band, and an unmoved press stays a click.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell object_tiles_drag_by_their_whole_body_and_instruments_do_not"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-2-body-drag-20260831 ]
        }
        check browse-navigation {
            statement """
                The toolbar breadcrumb browses to an ancestor and the Files button hands the open folder to the standalone manager.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell -- toolbar_breadcrumb toolbar_files"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-2-browse-navigation-20260831 ]
        }
        check gates-green {
            statement """
                The full repository gate passes with all of the above merged.
                """
            method command
            command "just check"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-2-gate-20260831 ]
        }
        check hands-on-confirmation {
            statement """
                At a real seat: a new window opens centred and can be moved by its top band and resized by its corner grip; the tiling menu visibly arranges; tiles drag-move; the Settings widget opens Settings.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check placement-policy {
            statement """
                An origin-located map request is centred and cascaded wholly inside the usable area; an oversized one is clamped; a positioned request is honoured and repaired.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-window -- centred cascade clamped honoured"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-2-placement-20260831 ]
        }
        check settings-widget {
            statement """
                One Settings widget replaces the battery/volume/brightness tiles, shows their state, and its open action launches the Settings app; saved layouts migrate.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell settings"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.settings-widget-consolidation-20260831 ]
        }
    }
    derived_from [ @legeos.observation.hands-on-run-20260831-findings ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-surface-usability-next ]
}

record legeos.work.hands-on-run-2-fixes/2 : work {
    title "Act on the second hands-on run: adjustable windows, visible tiling, body-drag tiles, concise labels, a route to drives, one Settings widget"
