record legeos.work.hostd-deployments-follow-the-layout-20261002/1 : work {
    title "hostd stages candidates at @deployments/<id> and its boot entries name that subvolume, as layout.toml declares"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "cli/templar/src/dev/gates.rs",
        path "distro/deploy/README.md",
        path "distro/deploy/layout.toml",
        path "installer/provision.sh",
        path "services/templar-hostd/**",
        path "tests/integration/provision-qemu.sh"
    ]
    intent """
        Fix @legeos.observation.hostd-stages-candidates-outside-the-declared-deployments-subvolume.
        - hostd's real configuration derives the deployments location from layout.toml's subvolume_template and the /.deployments mount the provisioner writes, not from state_dir.join("deployments"); the mounted directory (where snapshots are created) and the btrfs subvolume path (what rootflags=subvol= names) are two separate values in Deployment, never one path printed twice.
        - Boot entries for GRUB and systemd-boot carry subvol=@deployments/<id> for a candidate and the known-good deployment's own subvolume (initially @) for the fallback.
        - hostd's registry and transaction ledger stay in /var/lib/templaros/hostd (they are State tier); only the snapshots move.
        - templar dev deploy's root-before-<set> snapshot is either taken into @deployments as a deployment hostd knows, or listed as a declared exception in step 1's table, not left as a second, silent rollback store.
        """
    note """
        Independent of the decision's open choices: this is the layout the project already declared. Verified with fixture trees and the provisioner's disk-image path; a staged candidate actually booting is a user-run gate on hardware.
        """
    acceptance {
        check candidate-boots-on-hardware {
            statement """
                On the reference laptop, a hostd-staged candidate boots from @deployments/<id>, reports its deployment id, and the known-good entry still boots.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check config-from-layout {
            statement """
                A test builds hostd's real configuration over a fixture root and finds the deployments directory and subvolume template from layout.toml; changing the template in the fixture changes both.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p templar-hostd deployments_follow_the_layout"
        }
        check entries-name-the-subvolume {
            statement """
                For a staged candidate, the GRUB and systemd-boot entry writers emit rootflags=subvol=@deployments/<id> and the fallback names the known-good subvolume; no entry names a /var path.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p templar-hostd boot_entries"
        }
        check image-path {
            statement """
                The provisioner's disk-image run creates @deployments and a staged candidate lands inside it, or the script reports not-executed with its reason.
                """
            method command
            command "tests/integration/provision-qemu.sh"
        }
    }
    derived_from [
        @legeos.observation.hostd-stages-candidates-outside-the-declared-deployments-subvolume
    ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.ownership-tiers-20261002 ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.hot-corner-fullscreen-reveal-and-a-centred-island-20260908/1 : work {
    title "The bottom-left corner is Home, fullscreen gets the switcher back on a dwell, and the island stops sitting in the corner"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "compositor/COMPOSITOR.md",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/input.rs",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/protocols_shell.rs",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/state.rs",
        path "crates/templar-window/src/geometry.rs",
        path "crates/templar-window/src/service.rs",
        path "interfaces/wayland/templar-shell-v1.xml",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/surface/app.rs",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/wayland_bridge.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        Three things the user asked for on 2026-09-08 that the shell cannot do alone, because while a window owns the pointer the shell never learns where the pointer is.

        1. A bottom-left hot corner reveals Home. "I would prefer a bottom left hot corner for showing the home screen, not a button" — this replaces the Home chip removed in @legeos.decision.one-persistent-bottom-bar-tags-not-bands/6, whose only surviving pointer route is the Field's own context menu, which a covering window hides.

        2. Fullscreen auto show/hide. "auto show/hide in full screen, and always there on the home screen itself." This reverses rev 5's deletion of the bottom-edge peek: a visible fullscreen client window sorts above the shell overlay, so the compositor has to raise the overlay on a dwell. The deleted machinery is recoverable verbatim from commit 0b6d8fc (update_bar_peek / finish_bar_peek / peek_output_at / in_peek_band, WindowService::{peek_output,set_peek_output,is_peeking}).

        3. The island moves off the corner. The island now sits at the bottom-left because a zero-size zone claim anchors a surface at the start of its edge, which is exactly where the hot corner has to be — the two would fight over the same pixels. The fix is an additive alignment on the shell protocol (start / centre / end along the anchored edge) so the island can be centred the way the user's cosmic dock is, with the corner left to Home.

        As built, 1 and 2 are one dwell mechanism with two intents, and the two regions are disjoint by construction rather than by a precedence rule: the corner square is Home everywhere and always (a fullscreen window included, because with no Home chip on the bar it is the only pointer route there), and the peek band is the bottom edge excluding that square. The corner is instead suppressed while a visible ShellOverlay surface is under the pointer, which makes item 3 a hard prerequisite of item 1 rather than a cosmetic improvement on it: until the shell centres its island, its collapsed 72x6 hint tab sits on top of the 8x8 corner square and the corner cannot fire.
        """
    note """
        One dwell mechanism, two intents, both hung off the single place the compositor already sees the pointer in global logical coordinates (`update_perimeter_cursor`'s call sites in both motion paths). Item 3 adds a Wayland request, so the interface version bumps — but there is no Wayland baseline to re-freeze: `interfaces/baseline.json` freezes D-Bus signatures only and `xtask check-interfaces` walks `interfaces/dbus/`, so the gate for a protocol change here is the build (wayland-scanner generates from the XML), SHELL_PROTOCOL_VERSION on both peers, and the crate tests. All three need a logout: lege-comp is Restart=no.
        """
    acceptance {
        check corner-and-island-do-not-fight {
            statement """
                On hardware after a logout: the hot corner reveals Home without revealing the island, and reaching the island does not reveal Home.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check fullscreen-reveal {
            statement """
                A dwell on the bottom edge of an output carrying a visible fullscreen window raises the shell overlay above it, and leaving the edge lowers it again; nothing reflows either way because no zone changes.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-comp -p lege-window"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hot-corner-and-peek-dwell-tests-20260908 ]
        }
        check hot-corner {
            statement """
                Resting the pointer in the bottom-left corner reveals Home, from a bare desktop and from under a maximized or fullscreen window alike; sweeping through the corner does not, and neither does a drag released there.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-comp -p lege-window"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hot-corner-and-peek-dwell-tests-20260908 ]
        }
        check island-placement {
            statement """
                A bottom-anchored shell surface can ask to be centred along its edge; the zero-size claim still reserves nothing, and check-interfaces and check-interface-signatures both pass.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo run -q -p xtask -- check-interfaces && cargo run -q -p xtask -- check-interface-signatures"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.edge-alignment-placement-and-interfaces-20260908 ]
        }
    }
    implements [ @legeos.decision.one-persistent-bottom-bar-tags-not-bands ]
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.developer-edition-0-1 ]
}

record legeos.work.in-os-hotfix-from-templaros-20260911/1 : work {
    title "A hotfix path that updates installed TemplarOS, not the Lubuntu overlay session"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "cli/templar/src/doctor/checks.rs",
        path "installer/CHECKLIST.md",
        path "installer/README.md",
        path "justfile",
        path "scripts/update-templaros.sh",
        path "tests/integration/update-templaros.sh"
    ]
    intent """
        When TemplarOS is the running operating system, a developer can rebuild the native package set from a checkout and install it onto that OS without going through scripts/reinstall-templaros-desktop.sh, which is the Lubuntu overlay tester and must refuse to be confused with an OS update. scripts/update-templaros.sh is that path: it requires ID=templaros, refuses a casper live session, builds with just deb, and deploys through sudo templar dev deploy against /var/lib/templaros/devrepo so the install is one pinned apt transaction with a btrfs root snapshot. Kernel, NVIDIA and inherited Ubuntu packages stay on apt/templar update; this script is native-set hotfixes only.
        """
    note """
        Needed so an install from the 2026-09-09 ISO (gc2403fa, already on the SanDisk Ultra) can catch up to HEAD after first boot without rebuilding the medium.
        """
    acceptance {
        check accepts-installed-os {
            statement """
                With ID=templaros and no casper.conf, --check-host exits 0.
                """
            method command
            command "tests/integration/update-templaros.sh"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.update-templaros-host-gates-20260911/1 ]
        }
        check refuses-live {
            statement """
                With ID=templaros and a casper.conf present, the same check exits non-zero and says the live medium is ephemeral.
                """
            method command
            command "tests/integration/update-templaros.sh"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.update-templaros-host-gates-20260911/1 ]
        }
        check refuses-lubuntu {
            statement """
                On a host whose os-release is not ID=templaros, scripts/update-templaros.sh --check-host exits non-zero and names scripts/reinstall-templaros-desktop.sh as the overlay path.
                """
            method command
            command "tests/integration/update-templaros.sh"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.update-templaros-host-gates-20260911/1 ]
        }
    }
    after [ @legeos.work.install-onto-the-laptop-partitions-20260909 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.developer-edition-0-1 ]
}

record legeos.work.index-children-parent-id-contract-20260909/1 : work {
    title "Deferred — Index::children by an indexed parent lookup, once parent_id is correct on every path and the read views have a contract"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "crates/templar-file-index/src/lib.rs",
        path "crates/templar-file-index/src/mutation.rs",
        path "crates/templar-file-index/src/query.rs",
        path "crates/templar-file-index/src/reconcile.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        crates/lege-file-index/src/lib.rs Index::children (~575-598) retrieves and decodes the whole descendant range and filters immediate children in Rust, so recursive reconciliation pays for every descendant at every level. An indexed parent lookup needs parent_id correctness first: take-on-trust reconciliation observes directories with parent None, and mutation::place_at does not update parent_id on a move. Search/query reads and cursor row materialisation also use distinct live views. Write the contract (parent_id is set on every committed entry; a query and its cursor materialise from one view), fix the two writers, measure the reconcile workload against @legeos.observation.reconciliation-cost-tracks-tree-size-not-change-size, then switch children to the indexed lookup.
        """
    note """
        Astra: P2 deferred structural efficiency; explicit contracts and workload measurement, not incidental changes in the initial fixes. Follows the subtree-truth fix since both touch generation commits.
        """
    acceptance {
        check children-measured {
            statement """
                A reconcile benchmark on the fixture tree records the before/after cost of children lookups as evidence.
                """
            method observation
        }
        check parent-id-invariant {
            statement """
                Tests: every committed entry has a parent_id after take-on-trust reconciliation, and a move updates it.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p templar-file-index --test reconcile"
        }
    }
    after [ @legeos.work.subtree-repair-preserves-root-truth-20260909 ]
    depends_on [ @legeos.observation.reconciliation-cost-tracks-tree-size-not-change-size ]
    derived_from [
        @legeos.assessment.astra-memory-polling-indexing-review-20260909#children-scan
    ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.memory-polling-indexing-effectiveness-20260909 ]
}

record legeos.work.index-chunked-subtree-rename-20261009/1 : work {
    title "Chunked subtree rename application"
    state proposed
    intent """
        Split MoveDirectory application into bounded descendant batches (e.g. 2k rows per transaction) instead of one transaction rewriting every descendant path. A rename of a 100k-file tree currently holds the writer and grows one huge transaction; chunking bounds turn latency and WAL pressure while keeping each chunk atomic.
        """
    note """
        Deferred from the 2026-10-09 resource batch: medium complexity with atomicity/observability semantics to settle (partial-rename visibility across chunks, crash mid-chunks, change-log shape). Per-commit batching already narrowed the common case to watcher-scale renames.
        """
    part_of [ @legeos.work.file-index-maintenance ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.index-hdd-maintenance-pacing-20261009/1 : work {
    title "HDD-aware maintenance pacing"
    state proposed
    intent """
        Pace index maintenance for rotational media: detect rotational backing (e.g. /sys/block/*/queue/rotational for the database device) and use a slower checkpoint/maintenance cadence with larger batch windows, so HDD machines do not pay SSD-tuned fsync/checkpoint frequency as seek storms.
        """
    note """
        Deferred from the 2026-10-09 resource batch: needs a product decision (which devices qualify, exact cadences) plus a detection path that is honest on overlays, loopback, and network mounts rather than guessing.
        """
    part_of [ @legeos.work.file-index-maintenance ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.index-integrated-search-gui-20261008/1 : work {
    title "Future integrated Index1 search GUI with a large FSearch-style window"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "apps/**",
        path "crates/templar-session-core/src/providers.rs",
        path "distro/**",
        path "docs/indexing-dev/**",
        path "shell/templar-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Owner direction 2026-10-08: build an own integrated Index1 search GUI with a large FSearch-style window. Use the shared service for query, paging, generation and freshness rather than recreating a private index. Define the concrete application/UI/provider plan before implementation; preserve native-byte actions and honest retained-result bounds. The current FSearch fork remains a qualified prototype. The original WP14 shell/FSearch generation comparison and WP16 fork adoption are deferred; this proposed follow-up is not an implemented or accepted consumer.
        """
    note "Requested as future direction while the current parent continues independent index, Silvaview, crash and WP17 closure work. No agent deployment or live-session changes."
    depends_on [ @legeos.work.index-wp7-wp8-20261008/1 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.silvaview-and-fsearch-share-the-index/1 ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.index-lazy-search-overlay-20261009/1 : work {
    title "Lazy search-overlay refresh by tier visibility"
    state proposed
    intent """
        Make request_search_overlay_updates lazy: only roots whose tiers_for includes a visible/search tier pay for overlay refresh per commit; Unlisted-only roots skip it. The overlay exists to serve search visibility, so refreshing it for tiers no query can return is pure overhead on every apply.
        """
    note """
        Deferred from the 2026-10-09 resource batch: needs a check of the tier/visibility contract (which tiers queries can actually return) before narrowing the refresh, otherwise search results could go stale for covered roots.
        """
    part_of [ @legeos.work.file-index-maintenance ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.index-noop-reconcile-guard-20261009/1 : work {
    title "Skip generation publish on no-op reconciles"
    state proposed
    intent """
        Skip publish_generation (and its signals + overlay refresh) when a reconcile commit changed nothing: compare staged row count / content hash against the live generation before publishing, so no-op reconciles cost a scan but no generation advance, no consumer wakeups, and no WAL checkpoint pressure.
        """
    note """
        Deferred from the 2026-10-09 resource batch: generation-advance expectations are load-bearing (consumers key cursors and freshness off generations); skipping advances needs care to prove no consumer depends on the heartbeat.
        """
    part_of [ @legeos.work.file-index-maintenance ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.index-offline-consumer-actions-20261008/1 : work {
    title "Fence Silvaview known-offline native actions"
    state superseded
    scope [ path "distro/forks/silvaview/**", path "docs/measurements/**" ]
    intent "Fence known-offline Silvaview service-tree file-manager actions during WP17 continuation. Preserve cached display and native clipboard paths; prevent opening an indexed path under an offline root or while the source is loading/failed. Implementation belongs to the owning ../Silvaview-rs repository, with actual commit/source hashes retained; no live desktop or external file manager is launched in fixtures. Preserve existing user Cargo profiles and screenshot."
    acceptance {
        check guarded-native-actions {
            statement """
                Pure GUI target tests refuse known-offline/loading/failed actions, permit ready available native paths, and preserve feature-off builds.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test --features templaros --lib; cargo test --no-default-features --lib"
        }
        check offline-projection {
            statement """
                Service snapshot decoding retains native offline-root action bounds while leaving the cached logical-size tree and freshness visible.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test --features templaros --lib"
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @legeos.work.index-wp15-silvaview-20261008/2 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.silvaview-and-fsearch-share-the-index/1 ]
    author "dk"
}

