record legeos.work.low-memory-wallpaper-switcher/1 : work {
    title "Low-memory wallpaper switcher: new policy subcrate, temporary decoder and compositor-owned pixels"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "apps/templar-settings/**",
        path "cli/templar/**",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/**",
        path "crates/templar-wallpaper/**",
        path "docs/planning/low-memory-wallpaper-switcher.md",
        path "interfaces/**",
        path "services/templar-sessiond/**",
        path "shell/templar-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Implement crates/templar-wallpaper in the LegeOS workspace entirely in Rust: feature-light policy hosted by existing templar-sessiond, a temporary Rust-codec worker and compositor-owned static textures. Deliver startup restore, local random/sequential/shuffle selection, timed/manual/paused rotation, six physical sizing modes, per-output configuration and Settings/CLI/History controls, with no decoded cache, fade, preload or additional native resident daemon. Retain source-sized or explicitly reduced textures instead of expanding small sources into full-output wallpaper bitmaps. Deliver independently runnable X11 one-shot, generic layer-shell and portal adapters.
        Port the substantive recovered WUDB.cpp mathematical WuDP pipeline to dependency-light Rust, not the conceptual wudbquantizer.h placeholder or distinct speed-forked NeuQuant. Preserve LAB conversion, weighted PCA, projection histogram, contiguous dynamic-programming palette and CIEDE2000 mapping, with bounded histogram/scratch, deterministic tie handling and direct indexed output. Remove OpenCV/Eigen/vivid, C/C++ adapters, elastic probing, tolerance-based hash equality, random sampling and unbounded mapping caches. Specify new Rust parameters and simplifications; do not infer numerical results or exact tested source revision from the owner's prior report that WuDP did better. Newly authored Rust follows workspace licensing; preserved external sources have no explicit license notice.
        The owner's 2026-10-06 instruction supersedes the prior opt-in default: use 256-color WuDP by default if actual load overhead is not egregious, accepting modest additional load time because wallpaper changes are infrequent. Measure optimized full-size inputs; keep explicit null/off configuration and existing opt-outs, finite worker/transition budgets and real R8-plus-palette storage without an RGBA mirror. Document observed lossy banding; neither default selection nor logical texture-byte savings establish a full quality/comparator or physical-GPU/Variety release claim. Rust-only decoder requirement supersedes the earlier optional C/libjpeg adapter; earlier libjpeg measurements are historical, not Rust decoder evidence. Conservative preflight and measured worker peaks must account progressive coefficients and nonstreamable formats. Retain authenticated sealed-FD/generation/overlap and actual-frame presentation contracts. Matched Variety, full quantizer comparison and physical/GPU release gates remain explicit observations to collect, not fabricated from successful compilation or offline indices. See docs/planning/low-memory-wallpaper-switcher.md.
        """
    note """
        Original report preserved as wallpaper-report-export-20260911, SHA256 7b931e593c4584a6ceea84bc74903f6666bb8e4422c1eaf7ec87dec593ee5af9; normalized report as low-memory-background-switcher-20260911, SHA256 541a809a37c9ca1c7c5059aa38c471822fa0336fc93753dccad643086f3a5ad7. Metadata timestamp 2026-09-11T03:02:36.827090Z and backing_conversation_id 6aa36e6a-16b0-83ec-a496-d8d4379c84da do not establish a direct conversation URL/title. Root copy removed only after archive verification.
        Adopt backend-specific ownership, no decoded cache, temporary decoder, startup/sizing/rotation and separate process/shared/graphics accounting. Native Home needs one alpha-correct presenter rather than retaining old and new presenters. Rust workspace package replaces mandatory standalone C; native compositor textures replace unavailable Templar layer-shell; bounded transactional overlap replaces indefinite buffer-release waits; progressive coefficients remain budgeted despite scanline output; matched Variety gates replace a five-minute completion deadline.
        Native baseline/progressive JPEG decoder observations are documented in docs/measurements/wallpaper-decoder-20261006.md; no wallpaper/Variety/GPU claim follows. No live session or service was changed.
        WuDP recovery 2026-10-06: Second/misc loose filename searches and selected source archives found none; 2015.arc could not be listed. New red-drive spelling-adjacent files actually declare WuDPQuantizer. WUDB.cpp has SHA256 2a1cdfbd63a90ef6a9a2a6b5e237d784a703722197e5bb6d48ef3ca2dd5fe191; wudb.h e1cf903d543ca450e6f3fbae1144591d5c06a4a103778a97ef5b849a049d73bb; wudbquantizer.h 1dbc02c572b538deeb20e968e041ec4204d0dc2612689e8d2da0368b58fe3024. All three AKR source copies were byte-compared equal to originals, which remain unchanged. The conceptual wrapper's frequency-sort placeholder is not the substantive algorithm. A native c++ -std=c++17 -fsyntax-only probe of unchanged WUDB.cpp failed at missing WuDPQuantizer.h; header field/constructor differences are also visible in source. This identifies the algorithm family, not the exact previously tested revision. No comparative benchmark rerun.
        """
    acceptance {
        check bounded-memory-lifecycle {
            statement """
                One worker and latest pending job, validated sealed-FD transport, no decoded/preload cache, old/new overlap within declared byte limits; all children reaped and obsolete mappings/textures released across 100 changes, cancellation, source errors, output/context loss and owner restart. Progressive JPEG and other nonstreamable sources honor the explicit worker envelope or fail clearly.
                """
            method observation
        }
        check compatibility-backends {
            statement """
                Owned X11 setter exits between changes, checked stripe reuse/root publication does not leak pixmaps or kill unrelated clients; generic layer-shell honors configure/release and cannot indefinitely stall rotation under release starvation; portal reports unsupported sizing/residency controls and owner acceptance honestly. No XWayland-root substitution or live-session deployment.
                """
            method observation
        }
        check native-visible-behavior {
            statement """
                Isolated native session visibly restores startup wallpaper; local rotation, Next/Previous/Pause/Resume and all six sizing modes work, including small JPEG-to-4K and multi-output transforms, with unchanged Home input/occlusion/fullscreen/lock/capture behavior. GUI, CLI, Reset and History share desired/applied state.
                """
            method observation
        }
        check quantization-disposition {
            statement """
                Use the recovered substantive WUDB.cpp WuDP algorithm, with coherent interfaces and established licensing, not the conceptual wrapper placeholder. Run the bounded WuDP-first comparison against distinct speed-forked NeuQuant, reduced/full RGBA and indexed-PNG control, with real indexed rendering where available. Declare K/histogram/probe/sampling/bin parameters, include K below 256 to exercise DP, bound caches/histogram and emit real indices without a full BGR/RGBA mirror. Preserve the owner's qualitative prior result without invented numerical claims or a confirmation rerun. Record actual memory, peak, quality and latency; enable only a measured acceptable indexed winner, or retain quantization off with evidence of why. Keep heavy dependencies in a temporary decoder, not resident policy hosts; do not duplicate a quantizer.
                """
            method observation
        }
        check reduced-texture {
            statement """
                Real native renderer retains small-source/reduced textures without a hidden full-size CPU mirror, actual output quality is inspected, per-context replicas and full-resolution scanout/capture are counted, and reduced mode improves attributable storage under its selected budget.
                """
            method observation
        }
        check variety-performance-memory {
            statement """
                Matched version/backend/process-tree Variety comparison over at least 100 startup/rotation samples: medians no worse than baseline and p95 <=1.10 times baseline; idle aggregate utility incremental PSS <5 MiB and <50% of baseline; publish host totals and separately account shell/shared/graphics/GPU storage and measured worker peaks. Missing GPU measurements are not claimed as whole-system savings.
                """
            method observation
        }
    }
    implements [ @legeos.constraint.services-not-indicators ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-field-settings-gui ]
    author "dk"
    source {
        kind external
        path "sources/external/low-memory-background-switcher-20260911--541a809a.md"
        excerpt """
            Original wallpaper design report, normalized with provenance.
            """
    }
    source {
        kind external
        path "sources/external/wallpaper-report-export-20260911--7b931e59.md"
        excerpt """
            Complete original JSON export; report preserved before root retirement.
            """
    }
    source {
        kind external
        path "sources/external/wudp-conceptual-header-20261006--1dbc02c5.md"
        excerpt """
            Recovered wudbquantizer.h: internal WuDPQuantizer name, explicit conceptual wrapper and placeholder.
            """
    }
    source {
        kind external
        path "sources/external/wudp-implementation-20261006--2a1cdfbd.md"
        excerpt """
            Recovered unchanged WUDB.cpp: WuDPQuantizer, LAB/PCA/projection-bin DP and CIEDE2000 BGR assignment.
            """
    }
    source {
        kind external
        path "sources/external/wudp-interface-20261006--e1cf903d.md"
        excerpt """
            Recovered wudb.h interface; not equivalent to NeuQuant and not a coherent build with the companion snapshot.
            """
    }
    source {
        kind internal
        path "docs/planning/low-memory-wallpaper-switcher.md"
        excerpt """
            Complete proposed architecture, memory lifecycle, compatibility, recovered WuDP analysis and release gates.
            """
    }
}

record legeos.work.lxqt-alternative-desktop-20261014/1 : work {
    title "Provide current LXQt as a selectable alternative to the native TemplarOS desktop"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "apps/templar-greeter/**",
        path "debian/**",
        path "distro/**",
        path "scripts/**",
        path "session/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Owner requested latest upstream LXQt as a usable login-screen alternative because Homegarden is inconsistent. Work runs on native Lubuntu 25.10; installed TemplarOS is an offline mounted Resolute 26.04.1 root. Preserve the live Lubuntu desktop; do not start or stop installed desktop services. Diagnose pointer selection and session launch, package integration reproducibly, install to the offline target when possible, and state physical-seat validation limits.
        """
    acceptance {
        check latest {
            statement """
                Latest verified upstream LXQt components and a window manager are packaged and installed in the offline TemplarOS target with matching session entry.
                """
            method observation
        }
        check launch {
            statement """
                Discovered X11 sessions receive an X server launcher and correct desktop/session environment; Wayland sessions keep their own compositor.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p templar-greeter"
        }
        check picker {
            statement """
                The greeter session popup supports pointer selection of LXQt without submitting authentication.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p templar-greeter"
        }
        check seat {
            statement """
                Owner can select LXQt at TemplarOS login, reach a complete desktop, log out, and return to the native session.
                """
            method manual
        }
    }
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.lxqt-alternative-desktop-20261014/2 : work {
    title "Provide current LXQt as a selectable alternative to the native TemplarOS desktop"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "apps/templar-greeter/**",
        path "debian/**",
        path "distro/**",
        path "scripts/**",
        path "session/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Owner requested latest upstream LXQt as a usable login-screen alternative because Homegarden is inconsistent. Work runs on native Lubuntu 25.10; installed TemplarOS is an offline mounted Resolute 26.04.1 root. Preserve the live Lubuntu desktop; do not start or stop installed desktop services. Diagnose pointer selection and session launch, package integration reproducibly, install to the offline target when possible, and state physical-seat validation limits.
        """
    note """
        Implemented and installed offline from native Lubuntu. Existing LXQt entry was supplied by lxqt-session, a dependency of native lxqt-policykit; popup rows overlapped Sign in and background input consumed LXQt clicks. The greeter now isolates modal input, forwards DesktopNames/session identity, and wraps X11 Exec with startx on the login VT. Rebuilt26 pinned source packages for LXQt2.4.0 (panel/PCManFM2.4.1, portal1.4.0) with Resolute Qt6.10.2, installed full desktop/Openbox/Xorg with templaros-lxqt and updated greeter. Defaults use installed Papirus icons; XScreenSaver is explicit. Runtime/package evidence is scoped: actual private GUI selection and LXQt startup/application rendering pass, but owner physical-seat login/logout/native-return acceptance remains required. Current source changes are uncommitted. Greeter clippy, fmt, seed generation and packaging checks pass; combined xtask clippy has six pre-existing idle-wakeups/index_load diagnostics, not new LXQt diagnostics.
        """
    acceptance {
        check latest {
            statement """
                Latest verified upstream LXQt components and a window manager are packaged and installed in the offline TemplarOS target with matching session entry.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [
                @legeos.evidence.lxqt-backport-offline-install-20261014,
                @legeos.evidence.lxqt-installed-owned-desktop-20261014
            ]
        }
        check launch {
            statement """
                Discovered X11 sessions receive an X server launcher and correct desktop/session environment; Wayland sessions keep their own compositor.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p templar-greeter"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.lxqt-greeter-selection-and-launch-20261014 ]
        }
        check picker {
            statement """
                The greeter session popup supports pointer selection of LXQt without submitting authentication.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p templar-greeter"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.lxqt-greeter-selection-and-launch-20261014 ]
        }
        check seat {
            statement """
                Owner can select LXQt at TemplarOS login, reach a complete desktop, log out, and return to the native session.
                """
            method manual
        }
    }
    supersedes [ @legeos.work.lxqt-alternative-desktop-20261014/1 ]
    author "dk"
    source {
        kind external
        role origin
        url "https://lxqt-project.org/releases/"
        use """
            Upstream LXQt2.4.0 and current panel/PCManFM point-release inventory.
            """
    }
}

