record legeos.work.pdf-homegarden-hdmi-20261007/1 : work {
    title "Owner PDF: contained project Home, sessions/Desktop dock and survivable HDMI"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "Cargo.lock",
        path "Cargo.toml",
        path "ci/**",
        path "cli/**",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/**",
        path "crates/templar-appd/**",
        path "crates/templar-build/**",
        path "crates/templar-client/**",
        path "crates/templar-field/**",
        path "crates/templar-session-core/**",
        path "crates/templar-types/**",
        path "debian/**",
        path "docs/**",
        path "helpers/templar-preview-codecs/**",
        path "interfaces/**",
        path "scripts/**",
        path "services/templar-filed/**",
        path "services/templar-hostd/**",
        path "services/templar-sessiond/**",
        path "session/**",
        path "shell/templar-shell/**",
        path "tests/**",
        path "tools/xtask/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Implement the owner's 2026-10-07 18-page PDF /home/dk/Downloads/Untitled.pdf, LegeOS: Home garden scoping and HDMI review. Parent rendered all pages and viewed proposed Home mock-up page5 and HDMI flow page13. Home: verified project linking, root/HOME-ancestor exclusion, no duplicate child Place, stable path-seeded placement, pin versus manual-resize semantics; one project object contains live/parked windows, coding/agent sessions, recent files/apps and template bodies, everything else in one Loose tray; active/resting/fading light, actionable text, attention-only color, Sessions/Files/Apps, safe Focus/Resume, genuine private shell journals/agent/editor adapters and stronger verified process-directory evidence. Independent live Desktop dock replaces machine-facts Files tile, native cross-client drag/drop and filed journalled copy/move/undo. HDMI: survivable shared session/greeter secondary bring-up recovery, deterministic render/feedback/primary output, TV-safe mode/8-bit formats, hotplug settle and bounded late EDID, bounded fence/capability handling, make-before-break/tolerant readback, primary-output callback pacing, genuine secondary driver/render worker isolation and lazy activation with honest power/suspend gates. Keep preview capture off secondary passes, extended-output semantics explicit, quality/naming/dependency-source closure updated. Preserve earlier Home click, nm-tray2, DateTime and name-tab layer repairs. Six parallel implementation slices use distinct ownership and one server and shell integration owner each; parent runs native isolated verification.
        """
    note "Latest owner direction defers native PixelKit picker and restores LXQt; this plan does not re-promote it. The October7 09:33:44UTC installed compositor2339 explicitly self-aborted after a thirty-second watchdog stall. The retained kernel sample shows its thread in uninterruptible folio/Btrfs page wait; global OOM killed the core collector, so this incident has no recovered user stack and must not be described as an observed Mesa glFenceSync stack. The older Mesa evidence and PDF multi-GPU hypothesis are separate incidents/hypotheses. Installed single-GPU behavior, unqualified checkout hardware paths and actual observed failure remain distinct. No live session/device/PAM/user-bus/clock/locale/network mutation or deployment. Physical Intel/NVIDIA/TV/suspend/installed acceptance remains unclaimed until actually observed. Existing service authority and frozen existing wire signatures remain; new capability members use additive versioned APIs. Strong PID/cgroup verification, no title/name privilege grants, no private agent store parsing or raw command/prompt defaults. Latest owner mock-up supersedes prior prohibitions on Home previews/window lists and directory-tree default bodies, not stable geometry/ledger/source/privacy invariants. All new delegated agents, including nested delegates, use Sol per the owner's continuation direction. Owner direction on 2026-10-07 indefinitely defers Code/VS Code integration: experimental sources retained but excluded from both packaging paths, no runtime acceptance claim or further Code work. Independently verified Neovim remains in scope."
    acceptance {
        check desktop-dock {
            statement """
                Actual Desktop dock updates from filed change feed, preserves migration/order/geometry, opens and previews files, accepts and originates native cross-client file drops, and journalled copy/move/collision/undo work on disposable files without garden growth.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [
                @legeos.evidence.desktop-order-authority-regressions-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.desktop-source-ui-independent-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-desktop-fileops-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-desktop-image-preview-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-desktop-native-image-open-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-desktop-native-incoming-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-desktop-native-outgoing-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-desktop-order-feed-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-desktop-order-undo-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.session-boundary-regressions-20261007/1
            ]
        }
        check hdmi-safety {
            statement """
                Production secondary driver work is isolated from input/event-loop, admitted fence paths are bounded and unsupported imports honest; recovery/epoch/primary ordering/TV mode/formats/hotplug/reprobe/transactions/readback/callback/lazy-device behavior have focused regression and owned runtime evidence. Physical qualification and power/suspend limits are reported separately, not inferred from software fixtures.
                """
            method observation
        }
        check integration-delivery {
            statement """
                Affected source builds and regressions, actual owned UI/worker journeys, additive ABI/actions/source closure/package gates and coherent packaging are observed; current docs/knowledge match owner direction, unrelated changes/live session remain preserved, AKR validates with diagnostics disclosed.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [
                @legeos.evidence.garden-refresh-integration-delivery-20261008/1,
                @legeos.evidence.garden-refresh-owned-home-20261008/1,
                @legeos.evidence.garden-refresh-packages-gates-20261008/1,
                @legeos.evidence.garden-refresh-shell-tests-20261008/1
            ]
        }
        check project-authority {
            statement """
                Owned real user-manager launches yield verified window identity and correct project attribution; root/HOME ancestors, child duplication, manual-size versus keep and categorical template hysteresis/override are exercised, forged or unknown identity gains no privilege.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [
                @legeos.evidence.identity-delivery-after-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.managed-startup-directory-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-resize-keep-unpin-20261008/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-template-hysteresis-20261008/1,
                @legeos.evidence.real-home-linking-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.real-kitty-session-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.session-boundary-regressions-20261007/1
            ]
        }
        check project-surface {
            statement """
                Actual PixelKit Home surface implements the page5 containment/light/actionable-text design at its representation rungs with previews on/off, one Loose tray, project drag-link and contained minimize/restore slots; all template/tab/Focus/Resume actions consume genuine data and earlier single-release behavior remains reliable.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [
                @legeos.evidence.current-effects-shell-regressions-20261008/2,
                @legeos.evidence.garden-refresh-owned-home-20261008/1,
                @legeos.evidence.garden-refresh-plain-recent-open-20261008/1,
                @legeos.evidence.managed-agent-hook-boundaries-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.managed-containment-feed-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.managed-home-single-click-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-current-home-actions-20261008/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-home-rungs-and-light-20261008/1,
                @legeos.evidence.owned-template-hysteresis-20261008/1,
                @legeos.evidence.real-home-linking-20261007/1,
                @legeos.evidence.real-kitty-session-20261007/1
            ]
        }
        check sessions-and-adapters {
            statement """
                Real isolated supported-shell command/pipeline/privacy journeys and actual hook payloads reach verified session rows, foreground collection runs only on tending/activation, safe brokered shell/agent resume works, editor folder hooks are runnable; private stores/raw prompts/arguments do not become default presentation data.
                """
            method observation
        }
    }
    part_of [ @legeos.work.developer-edition-daily-driver ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.pixelkit-should-carry-alpha-so-a-surface-can-be-a-shape/1 : work {
    title "pixelkit should carry alpha, so a shell surface can be a shape without painting it twice"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/previews.rs",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/surface/app.rs",
        path "shell/templar-shell/src/surface/bar_screen.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        Upstream work in the sibling `pixelkit` repository (`../pixelkit`, which has its own `.akr`), recorded here because LegeOS is the consumer that needs it and is currently paying for its absence.

        `pixelkit_raster::WindowBuffer` is `Vec<u32>` holding `0x00RRGGBB`, and `Painter::blend` takes alpha as a *weight* — `blend_channels(destination, source, alpha)` mixes colour channels and stores nothing in the top byte. There is no way to ask the painter what a pixel's coverage was, so a surface that wants to be a shape rather than a rectangle cannot get its alpha channel out of the toolkit that drew it.

        What LegeOS does instead, today: it renders the shape a second time, white on black, through the same `fill_rounded_rect_aa` primitive, and reads the low byte of that second buffer as coverage (`ShellApp::redraw_bar`, `BarScreen::opaque_shapes`, `ShmBuffer::write_masked`). It works and it is anti-aliased, but it is two rasterisations for one frame, it obliges every drawing surface to declare its solid shapes separately from painting them, and the two can drift apart — the comment on `opaque` says as much.

        What is wanted upstream: an alpha channel the painter maintains. Either `WindowBuffer` becomes premultiplied `0xAARRGGBB` throughout with `blend_channels` composing coverage rather than discarding it, or a `CoverageBuffer` is written alongside the colour one by the same primitives. The first is the honest one and the larger change; the second is closer to what LegeOS hand-rolls now and would let it delete the second pass without changing pixelkit's colour semantics.
        """
    note """
        Raised by the user on 2026-09-08 after the floating-island work: "we also need to improve pixelkit for alpha apparently". Not scheduled. LegeOS's mask pass is the workaround and stays until this lands; the `ponytail:` note in `bar_screen`'s module doc and the `opaque` field's doc are the two places that point at it.

        The sibling repositories are unpinned path dependencies (`@legeos.papercut.the-workspace-stopped-building-entirely-because`), so a pixelkit change lands in LegeOS the moment it is committed next door — with no version to hold it back. Pinning is owed before either of these moves.
        """
    acceptance {
        check no-visual-change {
            statement """
                The island's rendered pixels are unchanged across the switch: same rounded corners, same anti-aliasing, same premultiplied edges over the desktop.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check one-rasterisation {
            statement """
                The shell gets a frame's coverage from the painter that drew it, and `BarScreen::opaque_shapes`, the second mask pass in `redraw_bar` and the `bar_mask` buffer are all deleted.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell bar"
        }
    }
    derived_from [ @legeos.work.the-bar-floats-an-argb-surface-with-a-coverage-mask-20260908 ]
}

record legeos.work.pointer-grab-reentry-deadlock-fix-20261001/1 : work {
    title "A window-model change inside a pointer grab no longer deadlocks templar-comp: the pointer-focus refresh is deferred to the idle list"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/backend/check.rs",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/space_sync.rs",
        path "compositor/templar-comp/src/state.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        Fix the 2026-10-01 desktop freezes traced to Smithay 1ed69cb's PointerHandle holding its std mutex while a PointerGrab handles button/motion: a name-tag click (pins_on_click -> toggle_always_on_top) or a band drop reached space_sync::sync_after_change, whose refresh_pointer_focus locked the same mutex again on the same thread. sync_after_change now queues one pointer-focus refresh on the event loop's idle list (state.pointer_refresh_pending coalesces bursts) and the before/after pointer-scene comparison runs there, outside any grab.
        """
    note """
        Fix and regression test are in the working tree on top of 50af378 (uncommitted at completion). The deployed /usr/bin/templar-comp only gets it at the user's next deploy. The advisor's separate display-path weaknesses (needs_sync unchecked, no queued-frame completion deadline, unbounded screencopy before the display frame, unconsolidated repaint scheduling) are not part of this record.
        """
    acceptance {
        check grab-reentry-regression-test {
            statement """
                A test grab that changes the window model on button release returns, the loop dispatches the deferred refresh, and the grab has ended; the compositor and window crates' suites pass.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p templar-comp changing_the_window_model_inside_a_pointer_grab && cargo test -p templar-comp -p templar-window"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.pointer-grab-reentry-test-20261002/1 ]
        }
    }
    derived_from [ @legeos.observation.pointer-grab-reentry-deadlocks-the-compositor ]
    author "dk"
}

record legeos.work.project-semantic-service/1 : work {
    title "WS4 — projects as authoritative semantic objects; priority_boost becomes ProjectImportance"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "cli/lege/**",
        path "crates/lege-client/**",
        path "crates/lege-session-core/**",
        path "interfaces/**",
        path "services/lege-filed/**",
        path "services/lege-sessiond/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Identity phases 5-7. Projects1 is extended additively — no Projects2: Describe(id) returning project_json against interfaces/schemas/project.schema.json, ListDetailed, Update with an explicit key allowlist (unknown key refused, nothing stored), GetCurrent/SetCurrent (stored in settings_values under _internal.projects.current), SetState(active|archived) with archived projects still searchable and openable, AddLogicalApp(logical id + optional preferred variant), and Changed/CurrentChanged signals. The Project struct gains importance, state, created/last-opened/last-active timestamps and references, and loses the inert priority_boost — replaced by ProjectImportance { Normal, Important }; the JSON blob is serde-additive in both directions so no schema migration is needed. Open/close call Files.Recents1.SetProject/ClearProject, waking the dead Suggestion::CurrentProject in lege-filed. ProjectApp gains logical_app and last_variant; opening resolves preferred variant, then the logical default, then warn-and-skip, recording what launched. Importance reaches the governor without touching lege-resourced: an Important open project sets protected=true through the existing Resources1.SetInstanceHints on the instances it launched, restored on close or demotion. HomeField stores only presentation (this project is here, this size); the project service is the record of membership.
        """
    note """
        A graded importance channel is deliberately not built until resourced has a weight to multiply it by — the priority_boost lesson. CLI: lege project show / set --importance --state / current.
        """
    acceptance {
        check blob-compat {
            statement """
                An old project blob still carrying priority_boost loads with the value ignored; a new blob read by the previous binary round-trips without loss; apply_changes refuses an unknown key.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-session-core projects"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.ws4-blob-compat-20260901/1 ]
        }
        check update-roundtrip {
            statement """
                Update followed by Describe round-trips every allowlisted field through the D-Bus API, and SetCurrent reaches lege-filed's recents suggestion.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-sessiond projects"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.ws4-update-roundtrip-20260901/1 ]
        }
        check variant-reopen {
            statement """
                A project whose pinned flatpak variant was uninstalled reopens on the sibling variant and says so in history.
                """
            method manual
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.ws4-variant-reopen-20260901/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @legeos.work.logical-app-and-variant-identity ]
    implements [ @legeos.decision.representation-ladder-is-the-organizing-principle ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.design-consolidation-roadmap ]
}

