record legeos.work.resourced-signal-and-trace-bounds-20260909/1 : work {
    title "P2 — the governor's signal backlog and trace ring are bounded in bytes, with an explicit rule for what a full queue drops"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "services/lege-resourced/src/daemon.rs",
        path "services/lege-resourced/src/dbus.rs",
        path "services/lege-resourced/src/trace.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        services/lege-resourced/src/daemon.rs (~581, ~598-610) hands SignalEvents to the D-Bus task over an unbounded tokio channel; a stalled bus consumer turns the governor into a memory-pressure source. trace.rs (~103-108) bounds the ring by record count (5000 in production) while record size grows with the instance count. Bound the signal channel and write down the disposition rule: PressureChanged may coalesce to the latest level, NonMemoryStall diagnostics may drop oldest, but PressureAction must not be dropped blindly because cooperative trim and checkpoint delivery ride on that signal even though the executor reports applied. Give the trace ring a byte budget with an oversized-record policy (truncate detail, keep the header). Tests: a stalled consumer with a burst of ticks keeps the queue at its bound and every PressureAction is delivered; varying record sizes keep the ring under budget.
        """
    note """
        Astra rank P2, resource-daemon memory. ADR-0002 keeps D-Bus off the governor loop; the bound must never block the loop thread, so a try_send with the disposition rule, not an await.
        """
    acceptance {
        check signal-bound {
            statement """
                A stalled-consumer test holds the signal queue at its bound, delivers every PressureAction, and never blocks the loop thread.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-resourced daemon"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.effectiveness-1-scoped-tests-20260909/1 ]
        }
        check trace-byte-budget {
            statement """
                A test with records of varying sizes keeps the trace ring under its byte budget and applies the oversized-record policy.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-resourced trace"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.effectiveness-1-scoped-tests-20260909/1 ]
        }
    }
    derived_from [
        @legeos.assessment.astra-memory-polling-indexing-review-20260909#resourced-bounds
    ]
    implements [ @legeos.decision.resourced-separate-process ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.memory-polling-indexing-effectiveness-20260909 ]
}

